# M&A Intelligence Pipeline

Automated pipeline that extracts, classifies, and reports M&A activity 
from documents using n8n and Groq LLM.

## Workflow V1 — Conventional
![Workflow V1](images/workflow-v1.png)

## Workflow V2 — LLM Powered
![Workflow V2](images/workflow-v2.png)

## How It Works
1. Downloads PDF from Google Drive
2. Extracts text from the document
3. Chunks and scores content for M&A relevance
4. Extracts company names and roles (acquirer, target, advisor)
5. Classifies industries and flags IT/Tech deals
6. Generates a structured final M&A report

## Features
- Automatic PDF ingestion from Google Drive
- M&A relevance scoring and filtering
- Company name and role extraction
- Industry classification
- IT/Tech deal flagging
- LLM-powered detection via Groq (Llama 3.1)

## Tech Stack
- n8n (workflow automation)
- Groq API (LLM inference)
- Google Drive API
- Llama 3.1 8B

## Setup
Import either JSON file into your n8n instance and replace 
the following with your own credentials:
- Groq API Key (in the LLM - M&A Detector node)
- Google Drive credentials (in the Download File node)

## Use Case
Useful for analysts or researchers who need to quickly scan 
documents and surface M&A activity automatically.